        "title": "test(semver): add unit tests for semver-compare helpers",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe semver-compare helpers in `src/infra/semver-compare.ts` provide version parsing, normalization, and comparison used across package and plugin update logic. Despite all four exported functions being shared utilities, they had no unit tests.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdd unit tests for all four helpers:\n- `normalizeLegacyDotBetaVersion` — converts `1.2.3.beta.N` to `1.2.3-beta.N`, preserves standard semver\n- `parseComparableSemver` — parses standard/v-prefixed/null/invalid/legacy dot-beta versions\n- `comparePrereleaseIdentifiers` — stable outranks prerelease, numeric-before-string precedence\n- `compareComparableSemver` — major before minor before patch ordering\n\n## Changes\n\n- **`src/infra/semver-compare.test.ts`** — new test file covering all 4 exported functions\n\n## Evidence\n\nReproducibility: not applicable. This PR adds direct coverage for existing utility behavior.\n\nDirect behavior probe confirms correct parsing and comparison of standard, legacy, null, and invalid inputs.\n\n## Related\n\nN/A (self-contained test coverage improvement)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
